// EXPECT: [E011]
// EXPECT-TEXT: Error Ln 9, Col 12: this call closes a mutual-recursion cycle
// I.136. The recursion cycle closes through a FUNCTION POINTER: spin -> apply directly, apply -> spin
// through `f`. The cycle walk followed direct calls only, so no obligation was raised and spin(1) was
// ACCEPTED and ran out of stack. An indirect call is now an edge to every function whose address the
// program takes with a matching parameter count, and the cycle is ranked like any other: x passes
// through both calls unchanged, so nothing falls.
func apply(f *func(u8) u8, x u8) u8 {
    return f(x)
}

func spin(x u8) u8 {
    return apply(spin, x)
}

func main() i32 {
    return spin(1) as i32
}
